# GRASS-ASSET: the grass blade's look comes from the asset - a scanned blade atlas (Poly Haven CC0 grass_medium_02:
# albedo, normal, ORM, opacity) on an ordinary TwoSidedFoliage material - and the code only places, bends and
# sways the cards (owner 10-29: "not procedurally generated in code, taken from somewhere").
Дано run Scene "Open Scene FIELD_Barn.desce"
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Entity "Sun"
Дано --subject selection set SunElevation 20
Дано --subject selection set SunAzimuth 110
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,170,2500
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.15,-0.25,-1
Тогда-вид 1_eye camera at 1.7 m: the near blades carry the scan's texture (veins, ragged edge, dry tips from the albedo/mask), not flat single-colour strips
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,600,2500
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.15,-0.12,-1
Тогда-вид 2_high camera at 6 m: dense grass, then the cover of the same tone with no seam, the far lowland the tone of the near grass (not dark grey); mesh grass and blades one colour with the cover, whose colour the cook derives from the albedo maps (no CoverAlbedo in the .demat)
Когда run Entity "Sun"
Когда --subject selection set SunElevation 12
Когда --subject selection set SunAzimuth 171
Тогда-вид 3_backlit sun 12 deg high straight against the camera (azimuth 171 = the view's): blades and far cover glow through by the asset's subsurface colour
